      ],
      "source": "https://www.colorfulcolorado.com/plan-your-visit/salida/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Salida was named meaning \"exit\" in Spanish, referencing the river’s outflow into Bighorn Sheep Canyon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salida%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1880 the Denver & Rio Grande Railroad built a narrow‑gauge line up from Texas Creek, creating a station called South Arkansas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salida%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The SteamPlant in downtown Salida houses the regional library, a studio arts school, and hosts touring musicians.",
